# The Piper J-3 Cub's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/j3cub.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The Cub has no flaps at all, so nothing here names one. Its undercarriage is
# fixed and it sits on a tailwheel, and its propeller is fixed-pitch, so there
# is no gear lever and no pitch lever either. Nor is there an electrical
# system: no starter, no lights, and a wire float on the tank cap for a fuel
# gauge. Its panel is a throttle and a carburettor heat control, with no
# mixture lever to set, so those items are the pilot's to confirm.
#
# The stick back is a negative elevator command, which is why the two items
# that ask for it read as they do.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, and the wire float on the tank cap showing fuel
confirm Chocks in, brakes on, and someone at the controls
confirm Switches off and throttle closed while the propeller is pulled through
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle cracked a quarter of an inch
confirm Contact called, and the propeller swung by hand

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running and idling evenly
check fcs/elevator-cmd-norm <= -0.40 Stick held back to keep the tail down
confirm Weave the nose left and right, for nothing is visible straight ahead
confirm Brakes tried as she first moves, and the wind allowed for
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Trim set for take-off
confirm Harness tight, controls free and correct, and the strip clear both ways
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 1950.0 Full throttle, and 1,950 rpm or better standing still
confirm Tail lifted to the flying attitude as she gathers speed
check velocities/vc-kts >= 34.0 Let her fly herself off at about 34 knots

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle wide open
range velocities/vc-kts 43.0 55.0 Climb at 45 to 52 knots
check position/h-agl-ft >= 300.0 Three hundred feet before the first turn
confirm The nose lowered every few hundred feet to look ahead
confirm Oil pressure steady and the engine running evenly

phase cruise
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 1950.0 2250.0 Cruising rpm about 2,150
range velocities/vc-kts 55.0 72.0 Cruise at 58 to 68 knots
confirm Carburettor heat tried, and left on if the air is damp and cool
confirm Altimeter set, and the fuel float watched as it sinks
confirm Trimmed to hold her height, with a field always within gliding reach

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.10 0.60 Throttle back for the descent
range velocities/vc-kts 43.0 60.0 Glide at 45 to 55 knots
confirm Carburettor heat on before the throttle is closed
confirm The engine warmed every minute or so on a long glide
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure

phase approach
range velocities/vc-kts 42.0 55.0 Approach at 45 to 50 knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.50 Power well back on the approach
confirm Carburettor heat on, and the strip and its windsock in sight
confirm Sideslip off the height if she is high, for there are no flaps to help
confirm The approach flown in a gentle curve so the strip stays in view

phase landing
range velocities/vc-kts 32.0 45.0 Over the hedge at 40 knots, slowing to the stall
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.20 Throttle closed in the round-out
check fcs/elevator-cmd-norm <= -0.70 Stick coming fully back as she settles
confirm Three-pointed, or wheeled on if the wind is strong
confirm Held straight with the rudder as she slows

phase after-landing
check velocities/vc-kts <= 25.0 Clear of the strip and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/elevator-cmd-norm <= -0.40 Stick back again for the taxi
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back to a taxi power
confirm Carburettor heat cold, and the trim reset
confirm Chocks in and the brakes on before the switches go off
